1
00:00:11,190 --> 00:00:12,000
Thanks.

2
00:00:19,510 --> 00:00:20,320
What?

3
00:00:21,190 --> 00:00:22,670
You like my lighter that much?

4
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:26,190
The ouroboros has a bad meaning.

5
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,000
How so?

6
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:33,320
A lot of people see the ouroboros

7
00:00:34,520 --> 00:00:36,710
as a symbol of Nietzsche's "eternal recurrence".

8
00:00:37,960 --> 00:00:39,600
He believed that human life

9
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:41,520
is trapped in a cycle of self-destruction

10
00:00:42,560 --> 00:00:43,920
and endless suffering.

11
00:00:45,350 --> 00:00:47,470
So you read philosophy too, To.

12
00:00:48,520 --> 00:00:50,880
But why do you only look at one side of things?

13
00:00:53,110 --> 00:00:54,880
The ouroboros consumes itself,

14
00:00:56,280 --> 00:00:58,320
but it's also a symbol of rebirth.

15
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,920
Everyone lives in cycles,

16
00:01:02,350 --> 00:01:03,560
not just cycles of suffering.

17
00:01:04,920 --> 00:01:07,200
But suffering will always exist.

18
00:01:08,510 --> 00:01:10,120
Well, life is painful.

19
00:01:10,790 --> 00:01:11,760
There's no avoiding it.

20
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:14,950
I chose the ouroboros

21
00:01:15,070 --> 00:01:16,680
to remind myself

22
00:01:16,680 --> 00:01:18,560
why I chose this life

23
00:01:19,310 --> 00:01:21,560
and what I can gain after getting through it.

24
00:01:23,760 --> 00:01:25,680
You could've just lived as a rich heir

25
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:28,760
without a care in the world.

26
00:01:29,870 --> 00:01:32,000
So why did you choose to become a CEO

27
00:01:32,350 --> 00:01:33,920
and deal with piles of paperwork every day?

28
00:01:36,590 --> 00:01:39,280
Since when have gangsters become so philosophical?

29
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:41,680
You just haven't met enough people.

30
00:01:47,150 --> 00:01:48,510
Keep it for now.

31
00:01:48,510 --> 00:01:49,710
Then you won't have to keep borrowing one.

32
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:51,560
Give it back to me later.

33
00:01:54,070 --> 00:01:54,920
All right.

34
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:40,340
♪With you, it's like I can breathe again♪

35
00:02:40,770 --> 00:02:43,540
♪I can't live without this breath, this heartbeat♪

36
00:02:43,660 --> 00:02:46,450
♪Forever's too far, but you're right here♪

37
00:02:46,720 --> 00:02:48,880
♪Together we'll take on this jaded world♪

38
00:02:49,020 --> 00:02:51,860
♪With you, I'll cross the dark, outrun the pain, and run away♪

39
00:02:51,940 --> 00:02:56,020
♪Still believing in true love, no matter how naive, calling you♪

40
00:02:57,600 --> 00:03:00,810
♪I'm willing to wait♪

41
00:03:01,660 --> 00:03:04,500
♪I love you like you're a part of me♪

42
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:07,300
♪I want to share my life with you♪

43
00:03:07,940 --> 00:03:13,720
♪To love this deeply, I'll give a little more♪

44
00:03:14,070 --> 00:03:15,870
♪In this cold and gray city♪

45
00:03:15,950 --> 00:03:17,580
♪Through all the pain, I'll hold you. Is it true?♪

46
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:20,030
♪Pieces of our memories slowly fade♪

47
00:03:20,110 --> 00:03:20,690
♪Stay with me♪

48
00:03:20,830 --> 00:03:23,440
♪Do you remember the day we crossed paths?♪

49
00:03:23,520 --> 00:03:24,220
♪Stay with me♪

50
00:03:24,300 --> 00:03:27,140
♪Do you remember the forever we promised?♪

51
00:03:27,630 --> 00:03:29,640
♪Who's waiting for you to save them?♪

52
00:03:30,170 --> 00:03:32,680
♪My heart aches, breaks, and struggles on♪

53
00:03:33,210 --> 00:03:35,720
♪How can I hold on to everything in one moment?♪

54
00:03:36,440 --> 00:03:39,940
♪Stop blaming fate and learn to let it be♪

55
00:03:41,880 --> 00:03:43,640
[Ash]
[Episode 7]

56
00:03:51,470 --> 00:03:52,710
Come back to me.

57
00:03:52,910 --> 00:03:53,990
I can take care of you too.

58
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:56,800
Don't go.

59
00:03:56,800 --> 00:03:58,470
We can talk about everything else later, okay?

60
00:03:58,560 --> 00:03:59,590
Don't touch me.

61
00:03:59,710 --> 00:04:01,190
I have nothing to say to you.

62
00:04:01,590 --> 00:04:02,910
Please stay away from me.

63
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:04,910
Mr. Hui,

64
00:04:06,560 --> 00:04:07,590
what do you want with my fiancé?

65
00:04:09,190 --> 00:04:11,120
I don't care about Eastern Hall.

66
00:04:11,150 --> 00:04:13,280
I just want this cop dead.

67
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:14,310
Are you out of your mind?

68
00:04:14,470 --> 00:04:15,840
You know he's a cop,

69
00:04:16,120 --> 00:04:17,510
and you're still keeping him around?

70
00:04:17,680 --> 00:04:19,270
How I run Eastern Hall

71
00:04:19,870 --> 00:04:21,680
and who I keep around me are none of your business.

72
00:04:22,480 --> 00:04:24,240
Please take your people and leave.

73
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:28,240
This isn't over.

74
00:04:43,190 --> 00:04:44,630
Whatever you're thinking right now,

75
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:46,390
the answer is no.

76
00:04:48,240 --> 00:04:51,000
You mean we should just leave him at Eastern Hall?

77
00:04:51,070 --> 00:04:54,000
You heard Ho Tung Fong just now. She's clearly protecting Mr. Mok.

78
00:04:54,800 --> 00:04:56,000
He'll be fine.

79
00:04:56,270 --> 00:04:57,750
That woman, Ho Tung Fong,

80
00:04:58,390 --> 00:04:59,430
killed her own father

81
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:01,800
and uncle just to take power.

82
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:04,630
The longer Mok Fei Foon stays by her side,

83
00:05:04,870 --> 00:05:06,430
the more danger he'll be in.

84
00:05:06,750 --> 00:05:08,630
You don't know why Mr. Mok works for the Ho family.

85
00:05:09,270 --> 00:05:10,600
If you act rashly,

86
00:05:10,600 --> 00:05:12,160
there's no telling what could happen.

87
00:05:12,800 --> 00:05:13,600
That's true.

88
00:05:14,630 --> 00:05:16,480
But Ho Tung Fong is dangerous.

89
00:05:16,480 --> 00:05:17,600
That's a fact.

90
00:05:21,160 --> 00:05:23,270
We've been at odds with Eastern Hall for years.

91
00:05:23,390 --> 00:05:24,600
Things are already tense between us.

92
00:05:25,240 --> 00:05:26,800
If you keep interfering,

93
00:05:28,680 --> 00:05:30,240
Eastern Hall may start suspecting Mr. Mok,

94
00:05:30,750 --> 00:05:32,390
and it could cost him his life.

95
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:36,070
He can't stay at Eastern Hall.

96
00:05:36,950 --> 00:05:38,430
Do you want him safe,

97
00:05:39,070 --> 00:05:40,430
or do you just want to keep him by your side?

98
00:05:41,160 --> 00:05:42,160
Don't forget.

99
00:05:43,360 --> 00:05:44,950
He's Ho Tung Fong's fiancé now.

100
00:05:45,040 --> 00:05:46,360
So what if they're engaged?

101
00:05:50,390 --> 00:05:51,630
Then what are you planning to do?

102
00:06:04,040 --> 00:06:05,270
Go to Eastern Hall

103
00:06:05,680 --> 00:06:07,000
and take him away.

104
00:06:11,270 --> 00:06:12,430
How are you going to take him away?

105
00:06:13,630 --> 00:06:15,190
Break into his place and kidnap him?

106
00:06:16,040 --> 00:06:17,240
Or wait until he goes out?

107
00:06:18,240 --> 00:06:19,680
He's wanted by the police now.

108
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:22,480
He definitely won't be going anywhere alone.

109
00:06:23,630 --> 00:06:26,560
Are you going to fight through a whole crowd just to take him?

110
00:06:26,750 --> 00:06:28,000
Where are you going to hide him?

111
00:06:29,750 --> 00:06:32,240
How will you make sure Eastern Hall doesn't find out you took him?

112
00:06:33,190 --> 00:06:34,070
Raid their operations

113
00:06:36,160 --> 00:06:37,630
and force them to agree to my terms.

114
00:06:39,560 --> 00:06:40,480
With whose men?

115
00:06:40,950 --> 00:06:41,630
Sheng Tung.

116
00:06:41,630 --> 00:06:44,270
You've never got along with those uncles in Sheng Tung.

117
00:06:44,750 --> 00:06:47,270
You used to be able to keep them in line with Tin Ping's interests.

118
00:06:48,600 --> 00:06:49,390
But now?

119
00:06:50,750 --> 00:06:53,870
How long has it been since you went back to Tin Ping, To Gor?

120
00:06:54,950 --> 00:06:56,630
Whatever you do,

121
00:06:57,160 --> 00:06:58,870
you could end up putting Mr. Mok in danger.

122
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:02,070
I'm begging you. Let him go.

123
00:07:03,480 --> 00:07:06,600
Pain and happiness will always coexist.

124
00:07:11,360 --> 00:07:12,190
No matter what,

125
00:07:12,750 --> 00:07:14,040
he can't stay in Eastern Hall.

126
00:07:15,160 --> 00:07:16,750
Even if it's Ho Tung Fong,

127
00:07:17,360 --> 00:07:19,070
she can't keep him there forever.

128
00:07:22,800 --> 00:07:24,390
If you've made up your mind,

129
00:07:25,360 --> 00:07:27,870
figure out how to get the uncles on your side.

130
00:07:34,950 --> 00:07:37,750
Let's continue discussing the financial projections for Bayfront Metropolis.

131
00:07:42,750 --> 00:07:45,040
You finally decided to show up, CEO?

132
00:07:45,600 --> 00:07:46,680
I've rested long enough.

133
00:07:47,190 --> 00:07:48,600
Time to get back to work.

134
00:07:49,390 --> 00:07:50,240
Go on.

135
00:07:52,190 --> 00:07:53,000
Fine.

136
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:56,390
Let's continue discussing the revised project plan.

137
00:07:56,630 --> 00:07:57,510
Enough.

138
00:07:57,830 --> 00:07:59,560
Rejected. Next.

139
00:08:01,240 --> 00:08:03,950
We already approved this at the last meeting.

140
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:06,040
Then you made the wrong decision.

141
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:09,070
Vincent, have you been away so long

142
00:08:09,390 --> 00:08:11,000
that you've completely lost your head?

143
00:08:11,190 --> 00:08:12,480
You're the ones who've lost your heads.

144
00:08:13,070 --> 00:08:16,240
We're not scaling the project down,

145
00:08:16,360 --> 00:08:18,070
and we're not keeping it as it is either.

146
00:08:18,480 --> 00:08:19,950
We're scaling up.

147
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:21,830
Are you out of your mind?

148
00:08:21,950 --> 00:08:24,160
Given Tin Ping's current situation,

149
00:08:24,160 --> 00:08:26,190
we can barely maintain the current scale.

150
00:08:27,630 --> 00:08:31,600
Why did you want to scale down in the first place?

151
00:08:31,870 --> 00:08:33,030
To save money?

152
00:08:33,750 --> 00:08:35,480
Then what about the next project?

153
00:08:36,630 --> 00:08:38,600
We've spent so long preparing for this

154
00:08:39,150 --> 00:08:40,390
and put so much into it

155
00:08:40,390 --> 00:08:43,150
because we wanted to take the company to the next level

156
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:46,360
and secure more large-scale development projects.

157
00:08:51,030 --> 00:08:52,550
Scaling down

158
00:08:53,270 --> 00:08:55,270
completely defeats the purpose.

159
00:08:56,390 --> 00:08:57,360
It shows a lack

160
00:08:57,550 --> 00:08:58,440
of vision and ambition.

161
00:09:00,030 --> 00:09:01,390
Easy for you to say.

162
00:09:01,750 --> 00:09:04,360
Where are you going to find the money to scale up?

163
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:10,360
Thirty per cent. Give me a 30% stake in the Bayfront Metropolis project.

164
00:09:10,630 --> 00:09:13,000
I believe your father will agree to invest, right?

165
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:17,600
Only if I have control over the project's direction.

166
00:09:18,200 --> 00:09:19,000
Deal.

167
00:09:19,840 --> 00:09:20,750
Little brat.

168
00:09:23,870 --> 00:09:27,150
Stop all the projects related to scaling down.

169
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:29,030
Switch to researching a scale-up plan instead.

170
00:09:29,790 --> 00:09:31,550
I'll handle the funding.

171
00:09:32,360 --> 00:09:34,750
Also, terminate the contracts with all the contractors

172
00:09:34,750 --> 00:09:36,840
we signed for the scale-down plan.

173
00:09:36,960 --> 00:09:38,390
Replace them with the ones I chose before.

174
00:09:38,390 --> 00:09:38,960
Terminate them?

175
00:09:39,270 --> 00:09:40,600
Loek To, are you joking?

176
00:09:40,840 --> 00:09:42,270
We can't just terminate contracts because you say so.

177
00:09:42,270 --> 00:09:43,790
How am I supposed to explain this to my people?

178
00:09:44,150 --> 00:09:45,750
Uncle, calm down.

179
00:09:46,080 --> 00:09:48,600
Naturally, I'll have a better offer for everyone.

180
00:09:54,550 --> 00:09:55,840
What? No way.

181
00:09:56,080 --> 00:09:56,790
What's wrong?

182
00:09:56,790 --> 00:09:57,600
It's bad.

183
00:09:57,600 --> 00:09:58,960
Fei Piu and Kwan Gor are both in trouble.

184
00:09:59,150 --> 00:09:59,960
Oh, no.

185
00:10:02,080 --> 00:10:03,150
What's the situation now?

186
00:10:03,360 --> 00:10:05,790
Several shops in Tsim Sha Tsui and our waterfront base have been hit.

187
00:10:05,960 --> 00:10:07,840
The four warehouses in Kwun Tong were set on fire.

188
00:10:07,840 --> 00:10:09,360
The goods are soaked and unusable.

189
00:10:09,440 --> 00:10:10,240
How much did we lose?

190
00:10:10,440 --> 00:10:11,240
We can't estimate yet.

191
00:10:11,480 --> 00:10:12,630
But it seriously affects our shipments.

192
00:10:12,840 --> 00:10:14,000
Contact the factory immediately.

193
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:15,240
Tell them to send us another batch.

194
00:10:15,240 --> 00:10:16,600
No. We don't have enough time.

195
00:10:16,600 --> 00:10:17,790
No matter what, we have to make it happen.

196
00:10:17,790 --> 00:10:19,600
I can't delay the delivery to Dreamweaver.

197
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:21,150
The export volume of paper and ink

198
00:10:21,150 --> 00:10:21,960
is under very strict control.

199
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:23,390
We agreed on the quantity beforehand

200
00:10:23,390 --> 00:10:25,000
so they could supply us on time and in the right amount.

201
00:10:25,240 --> 00:10:27,150
If we place an urgent extra order, it won't work.

202
00:10:27,440 --> 00:10:28,670
Make it work.

203
00:10:28,790 --> 00:10:30,200
I need this batch of goods now.

204
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:32,030
We can negotiate the price.

205
00:10:32,550 --> 00:10:33,360
Understood.

206
00:10:34,080 --> 00:10:36,390
I'll handle the venues that were hit.

207
00:10:37,750 --> 00:10:39,480
Look into who did it as well.

208
00:10:40,240 --> 00:10:42,550
So many of our venues were hit at the same time.

209
00:10:42,840 --> 00:10:43,840
It had to be planned.

210
00:10:44,790 --> 00:10:46,790
Could it be people from my father and second uncle's side?

211
00:10:47,030 --> 00:10:47,840
Doesn't seem like it.

212
00:10:49,440 --> 00:10:50,960
Have you heard anything recently?

213
00:10:51,200 --> 00:10:52,440
Who might be targeting Eastern Hall?

214
00:10:54,030 --> 00:10:56,960
I think it can only be the people from Sheng Tung.

215
00:10:57,630 --> 00:10:59,750
Remember Hui who came last time?

216
00:11:00,150 --> 00:11:02,200
He kept pestering you to hand someone over.

217
00:11:02,790 --> 00:11:03,600
That's right.

218
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:05,550
Most of the venues attacked this time

219
00:11:05,600 --> 00:11:08,030
were taken from Sheng Tung.

220
00:11:08,240 --> 00:11:09,630
There's a good chance it was them.

221
00:11:11,600 --> 00:11:12,600
What do you think?

222
00:11:12,790 --> 00:11:14,670
I read their files when I was at the police station.

223
00:11:15,360 --> 00:11:16,270
They were clean.

224
00:11:17,550 --> 00:11:18,790
It doesn't seem like something they'd do.

225
00:11:19,600 --> 00:11:20,840
Why are you defending him?

226
00:11:20,840 --> 00:11:22,200
That's not what I mean.

227
00:11:23,030 --> 00:11:25,750
I'm looking at this from Eastern Hall's perspective.

228
00:11:26,240 --> 00:11:28,870
If we make a decision before we've figured things out,

229
00:11:29,030 --> 00:11:30,550
we might not catch the real culprit,

230
00:11:30,550 --> 00:11:31,750
and we'll end up offending Sheng Tung.

231
00:11:32,030 --> 00:11:34,030
In the end, Eastern Hall will be the one that loses.

232
00:11:34,200 --> 00:11:36,080
We'll know whether they did it or not

233
00:11:36,080 --> 00:11:37,440
once we bring him back and ask him.

234
00:11:37,550 --> 00:11:38,360
All right.

235
00:11:38,790 --> 00:11:40,480
Fan Shu and I will bring him back.

236
00:11:40,480 --> 00:11:41,270
No.

237
00:11:42,200 --> 00:11:42,910
You.

238
00:11:43,790 --> 00:11:44,960
You're bringing him back.

239
00:11:45,750 --> 00:11:46,550
No problem.

240
00:12:05,200 --> 00:12:06,670
Just as you predicted,

241
00:12:07,390 --> 00:12:10,600
the uncles have been unhappy with Eastern Hall for years.

242
00:12:11,150 --> 00:12:13,000
Now that they can openly strike back,

243
00:12:14,080 --> 00:12:15,480
they're happy to finally

244
00:12:15,600 --> 00:12:16,790
vent their anger.

245
00:12:17,030 --> 00:12:19,270
No one is complaining about changing the contractors anymore.

246
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:23,750
But Eastern Hall has clearly increased security at their bases.

247
00:12:24,670 --> 00:12:26,480
It'll be difficult to strike again in the short term.

248
00:12:27,030 --> 00:12:28,390
So they are getting scared.

249
00:12:29,790 --> 00:12:32,790
Tell the uncles in Sheng Tung to keep attacking their venues.

250
00:12:33,030 --> 00:12:35,030
Force them to hand Fei Foon over.

251
00:12:38,750 --> 00:12:39,960
That's easier said than done.

252
00:12:40,630 --> 00:12:42,480
Who knows what kind of person Ho Tung Fong is?

253
00:12:42,960 --> 00:12:44,390
If you push her too hard

254
00:12:45,360 --> 00:12:46,790
and things get heated,

255
00:12:47,440 --> 00:12:48,840
how long will this drag on?

256
00:12:50,390 --> 00:12:51,200
It doesn't matter.

257
00:12:51,960 --> 00:12:53,480
Even if I can't force Eastern Hall to comply,

258
00:12:54,240 --> 00:12:56,390
I want Fei Foon to know I'm here to save him.

259
00:12:57,960 --> 00:12:59,550
Step up the game tonight.

260
00:12:59,960 --> 00:13:01,150
Hit a few more of their venues.

261
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:02,390
Understood.

262
00:13:11,260 --> 00:13:13,610
[Ten o'clock. The restaurant. See you there.]

263
00:13:17,370 --> 00:13:19,690
[Rich Tea Flavour]

264
00:13:23,720 --> 00:13:24,240
Enjoy.

265
00:13:24,240 --> 00:13:25,030
Thanks, sir.

266
00:13:37,960 --> 00:13:38,750
Fei Foon.

267
00:13:39,550 --> 00:13:40,360
Mr. Hui,

268
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:43,720
Ms. Ho wants to see you.

269
00:13:44,360 --> 00:13:45,150
No rush.

270
00:13:45,720 --> 00:13:47,600
Finish your pineapple bun first.

271
00:14:04,150 --> 00:14:05,030
Mr. Hui,

272
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:06,200
we meet again.

273
00:14:08,240 --> 00:14:09,030
Ms. Ho,

274
00:14:10,840 --> 00:14:12,390
your way of doing things

275
00:14:13,120 --> 00:14:15,150
has certainly opened my eyes.

276
00:14:15,480 --> 00:14:17,630
Several Eastern Hall venues have been attacked recently.

277
00:14:20,360 --> 00:14:21,440
Did your men do it?

278
00:14:23,390 --> 00:14:24,360
So what if it was?

279
00:14:25,870 --> 00:14:27,270
You insisted on protecting that cop.

280
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:29,600
If you had handed him over earlier,

281
00:14:30,360 --> 00:14:31,440
none of this would've happened.

282
00:14:32,390 --> 00:14:33,270
So all you want

283
00:14:34,960 --> 00:14:35,750
is him?

284
00:14:35,960 --> 00:14:37,000
That's right.

285
00:14:38,080 --> 00:14:39,030
I make sure

286
00:14:39,750 --> 00:14:41,750
anyone who protects him pays the price.

287
00:14:42,600 --> 00:14:43,440
Keep beating him.

288
00:15:03,030 --> 00:15:03,840
Mr. Hui,

289
00:15:04,390 --> 00:15:07,030
I really don't know what grudge you think we have between us

290
00:15:07,520 --> 00:15:09,200
that makes you keep coming after me.

291
00:15:09,670 --> 00:15:11,000
Please stop.

292
00:15:11,600 --> 00:15:13,840
Don't think we won't dare to kill you.

293
00:15:21,200 --> 00:15:22,030
Ms. Ho.

294
00:15:23,910 --> 00:15:24,720
Keep going.

295
00:15:30,910 --> 00:15:32,630
There's no point beating him anymore.

296
00:15:36,240 --> 00:15:37,600
Why don't we just shoot him?

297
00:15:38,440 --> 00:15:39,630
That'll settle everything once and for all.

298
00:15:43,360 --> 00:15:44,550
Are you crazy?

299
00:15:45,870 --> 00:15:46,630
Mr. Lok,

300
00:15:47,150 --> 00:15:48,910
whether I kill one person or two people,

301
00:15:49,360 --> 00:15:51,150
the punishment is still life imprisonment.

302
00:15:51,480 --> 00:15:52,200
There's no difference.

303
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:53,750
This isn't just about you.

304
00:15:54,150 --> 00:15:56,080
He has an entire gang backing him.

305
00:15:56,480 --> 00:15:58,480
Are you trying to start a full-scale war between us?

306
00:16:00,270 --> 00:16:01,960
This man won't stop coming after us.

307
00:16:02,510 --> 00:16:04,550
How is that any different from a full-scale war?

308
00:16:04,910 --> 00:16:05,720
Ms. Ho.

309
00:16:06,550 --> 00:16:08,080
Since I had him brought here,

310
00:16:08,270 --> 00:16:09,720
I never planned to let him leave.

311
00:16:10,600 --> 00:16:11,390
Shoot.

312
00:16:13,150 --> 00:16:14,150
Ms. Ho...

313
00:16:15,030 --> 00:16:15,910
Shoot.

314
00:16:17,200 --> 00:16:18,200
Once I'm dead,

315
00:16:20,200 --> 00:16:22,550
your world will finally be clean.

316
00:16:52,240 --> 00:16:54,670
He won't bother us anymore.

317
00:16:58,870 --> 00:16:59,750
Take care of this.

318
00:16:59,840 --> 00:17:01,100
I know what to do.

319
00:17:01,100 --> 00:17:02,390
It won't implicate Eastern Hall.

320
00:17:24,790 --> 00:17:25,590
Fei Foon.

321
00:17:41,680 --> 00:17:42,480
Sit up.

322
00:18:11,070 --> 00:18:12,590
I told you not to follow me.

323
00:18:12,590 --> 00:18:13,550
You never listen.

324
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:31,440
Good thing I had the lighter.

325
00:18:32,590 --> 00:18:33,790
It blocked the bullet.

326
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:38,830
Does it hurt?

327
00:18:45,790 --> 00:18:47,270
You got hurt because of me last time.

328
00:18:49,200 --> 00:18:50,750
Consider us even now.

329
00:19:10,680 --> 00:19:12,000
I don't have much time.

330
00:19:13,750 --> 00:19:15,750
Once you get out, don't do anything reckless again.

331
00:19:15,750 --> 00:19:17,270
Don't come looking for me again. Got it?

332
00:19:19,070 --> 00:19:20,400
That's too hard.

333
00:19:21,400 --> 00:19:22,200
I can't do it.

334
00:19:30,500 --> 00:19:33,820
I'm sorry. I shouldn't have said those things about you.

335
00:19:33,820 --> 00:19:36,880
I shouldn't have hurt you. I'm sorry.

336
00:20:26,800 --> 00:20:29,950
♪We met at the wrong time, and the wind blows us apart♪

337
00:20:30,170 --> 00:20:33,430
♪Our love runs this deep, yet we met at the wrong time♪

338
00:20:33,560 --> 00:20:35,240
♪I know these feelings are hard to hide♪

339
00:20:35,270 --> 00:20:36,970
♪I know there's a line that's hard to cross♪

340
00:20:37,010 --> 00:20:40,080
♪But I just had to meet you♪

341
00:20:40,170 --> 00:20:43,250
♪We met at the wrong time, and fate pulls us apart♪

342
00:20:43,280 --> 00:20:46,940
♪Our love runs this deep, yet we met at the wrong time♪

343
00:20:47,090 --> 00:20:49,270
♪All I can do is pretend I don't care♪

344
00:20:49,310 --> 00:20:50,960
♪All I can do is keep my distance in the crowd♪

345
00:20:50,960 --> 00:20:52,750
What was your original plan?

346
00:20:53,880 --> 00:20:55,780
To take me back and lock me away?

347
00:20:58,960 --> 00:20:59,880
Something like that.

348
00:21:03,480 --> 00:21:06,200
Did it never occur to you that Ho Tung Fong might come after you?

349
00:21:13,750 --> 00:21:16,790
You said exactly the same thing as Tam Fung.

350
00:21:18,350 --> 00:21:20,880
Because if you had thought about it, you'd know it would never work.

351
00:21:27,590 --> 00:21:29,590
I really don't know what goes on in your head.

352
00:21:31,790 --> 00:21:32,550
You.

353
00:21:39,200 --> 00:21:40,350
You're all I think about.

354
00:22:22,960 --> 00:22:24,030
What happened?

355
00:22:24,110 --> 00:22:25,920
What went wrong with the counterfeit money shipment?

356
00:22:26,550 --> 00:22:27,880
The factory doesn't have enough raw materials.

357
00:22:28,350 --> 00:22:29,160
This time,

358
00:22:29,160 --> 00:22:30,480
I'm afraid we won't make the delivery deadline.

359
00:22:30,680 --> 00:22:32,440
Then we'll deliver whatever we have.

360
00:22:33,160 --> 00:22:34,350
We'll settle

361
00:22:34,350 --> 00:22:36,510
the remaining amount with interest.

362
00:22:37,270 --> 00:22:38,880
At the end of the day, business is about money.

363
00:22:39,550 --> 00:22:40,550
If it were that simple,

364
00:22:41,030 --> 00:22:42,480
we wouldn't be so worried.

365
00:22:43,680 --> 00:22:46,270
Do you know why we work with Dreamweaver?

366
00:22:47,240 --> 00:22:48,720
A gang next door

367
00:22:48,880 --> 00:22:50,310
once failed to deliver on time.

368
00:22:50,640 --> 00:22:51,680
They were only a month late,

369
00:22:52,110 --> 00:22:53,830
and Dreamweaver wiped out the entire gang.

370
00:22:54,110 --> 00:22:56,920
I brought Dreamweaver in to deal with my second uncle and my father

371
00:22:57,310 --> 00:22:58,880
because I didn't want to become the leader

372
00:22:58,880 --> 00:23:00,310
only to be controlled by others at every turn.

373
00:23:01,110 --> 00:23:02,030
If that's the case,

374
00:23:03,160 --> 00:23:04,550
I'd rather go to war with them directly.

375
00:23:05,440 --> 00:23:06,270
Ms. Ho,

376
00:23:06,960 --> 00:23:09,680
we know nothing about who is behind Dreamweaver.

377
00:23:09,920 --> 00:23:11,110
This would be too risky.

378
00:23:11,830 --> 00:23:12,640
Foon,

379
00:23:13,070 --> 00:23:14,110
what do you think?

380
00:23:14,240 --> 00:23:15,440
Going to war isn't a problem.

381
00:23:16,480 --> 00:23:18,110
But if we're really going to fight,

382
00:23:19,110 --> 00:23:21,070
we need to take out their leader directly.

383
00:23:25,160 --> 00:23:26,830
Getting Pedro to meet us won't be easy.

384
00:23:27,440 --> 00:23:29,920
Every time there's a handover, he only sends his men.

385
00:23:30,510 --> 00:23:33,160
The only time we met him in person was when we bought the printing plate.

386
00:23:33,720 --> 00:23:34,640
Then that's perfect.

387
00:23:34,960 --> 00:23:36,030
We'll tell him

388
00:23:36,030 --> 00:23:37,310
we want to buy another printing plate.

389
00:23:37,920 --> 00:23:39,680
If he's willing to do the deal,

390
00:23:40,550 --> 00:23:43,920
we'll continue working together peacefully.

391
00:23:44,880 --> 00:23:46,750
But if he refuses,

392
00:23:47,480 --> 00:23:49,510
we'll deal with him on the spot.

393
00:23:51,880 --> 00:23:52,640
Ms. Ho,

394
00:23:52,640 --> 00:23:53,440
think this through.

395
00:23:53,440 --> 00:23:54,880
We'll do it Foon's way.

396
00:23:55,830 --> 00:23:56,590
Lok,

397
00:23:56,590 --> 00:23:58,440
gather our men and get ready.

398
00:23:58,640 --> 00:24:00,160
I'll contact Pedro now.

399
00:24:01,440 --> 00:24:02,110
Fan Shu.

400
00:24:02,110 --> 00:24:02,920
Yes.

401
00:24:06,440 --> 00:24:08,640
You handled the Hui Loek To situation well.

402
00:24:10,200 --> 00:24:12,720
Unfortunately, his men still managed to rescue him in the end.

403
00:24:12,830 --> 00:24:15,000
Right now, Pedro is what matters most.

404
00:24:18,350 --> 00:24:19,160
Please take a look.

405
00:24:22,960 --> 00:24:24,200
Good. Let's go with this.

406
00:24:33,750 --> 00:24:35,160
You finally decided to show up?

407
00:24:37,590 --> 00:24:39,480
The venue I picked isn't bad, right?

408
00:24:39,880 --> 00:24:42,550
I've almost finished making all the wedding arrangements.

409
00:24:44,200 --> 00:24:45,270
I'm happy enough just seeing you

410
00:24:45,270 --> 00:24:46,400
back at company meetings.

411
00:24:47,350 --> 00:24:48,750
The venue is very well chosen.

412
00:24:50,070 --> 00:24:52,750
But we won't be needing it.

413
00:24:54,830 --> 00:24:56,160
What do you have in mind?

414
00:24:56,160 --> 00:24:57,200
Do you want a different venue?

415
00:24:59,350 --> 00:25:00,790
I want to call off the engagement.

416
00:25:03,640 --> 00:25:05,400
This isn't funny, you know.

417
00:25:05,480 --> 00:25:06,750
Your sense of humour needs work.

418
00:25:13,400 --> 00:25:14,400
You're serious?

419
00:25:15,750 --> 00:25:16,640
Yes.

420
00:25:17,960 --> 00:25:20,750
Our partnership deal remains unchanged.

421
00:25:21,160 --> 00:25:23,640
And I'll transfer an additional five per cent of Tin Ping's shares to you

422
00:25:24,200 --> 00:25:25,000
as compensation.

423
00:25:27,160 --> 00:25:27,750
What do you mean?

424
00:25:27,750 --> 00:25:29,240
Do you think you can settle this with money?

425
00:25:29,750 --> 00:25:32,350
Hui Loek To, you were the one who suggested this fake marriage.

426
00:25:32,550 --> 00:25:35,160
And now you're suddenly backing out?

427
00:25:35,350 --> 00:25:37,160
Have you thought about what people will think?

428
00:25:37,160 --> 00:25:38,960
Everyone knows about our engagement now.

429
00:25:38,960 --> 00:25:40,000
How am I supposed to explain this

430
00:25:40,000 --> 00:25:41,400
to my father or anyone else?

431
00:25:41,750 --> 00:25:43,960
And what will the tabloids write about me?

432
00:25:44,680 --> 00:25:45,550
Don't worry.

433
00:25:46,110 --> 00:25:47,750
I've already had the PR department

434
00:25:47,750 --> 00:25:49,750
bring in a top PR team to handle the fallout.

435
00:25:50,960 --> 00:25:51,480
Okay.

436
00:25:51,920 --> 00:25:53,070
Give me a reason.

437
00:25:53,680 --> 00:25:56,000
Is it because the So family's investment

438
00:25:56,000 --> 00:25:57,160
isn't enough for you anymore?

439
00:25:57,590 --> 00:26:00,070
Or are you planning something else and sacrificing me for it?

440
00:26:01,880 --> 00:26:03,200
I just can't do it.

441
00:26:05,400 --> 00:26:06,270
You can't do it?

442
00:26:07,590 --> 00:26:09,160
You knew from the very beginning

443
00:26:09,160 --> 00:26:10,830
that this was only ever a business arrangement.

444
00:26:11,350 --> 00:26:12,750
What part of that can't you do?

445
00:26:13,000 --> 00:26:14,880
All we had to do was have a wedding

446
00:26:14,880 --> 00:26:15,960
and put on a good show for everyone.

447
00:26:16,350 --> 00:26:18,030
After that, we'd live our own lives.

448
00:26:18,030 --> 00:26:19,350
We'd both get what we wanted.

449
00:26:19,350 --> 00:26:20,240
What's so hard about that?

450
00:26:22,350 --> 00:26:23,590
I promised him

451
00:26:24,480 --> 00:26:26,160
that I wouldn't make him unhappy again.

452
00:26:31,790 --> 00:26:33,070
Who is he?

453
00:26:33,070 --> 00:26:34,440
He's not from our circle.

454
00:26:42,590 --> 00:26:47,350
Someone who could make Hui Loek To put Tin Ping Group second...

455
00:26:50,070 --> 00:26:51,400
You must really love him.

456
00:26:56,590 --> 00:26:57,960
He made me realise

457
00:26:58,440 --> 00:26:59,880
that there are things

458
00:27:01,160 --> 00:27:03,750
more important than work that are worth fighting for.

459
00:27:07,440 --> 00:27:08,240
Okay.

460
00:27:09,880 --> 00:27:11,160
Since you've made up your mind,

461
00:27:11,240 --> 00:27:12,750
there's nothing I can say to change it.

462
00:27:14,640 --> 00:27:16,590
As for why the engagement is off,

463
00:27:17,240 --> 00:27:19,000
you'll have to explain it to my father yourself.

464
00:27:19,240 --> 00:27:20,030
Okay.

465
00:27:22,030 --> 00:27:24,200
So, if people ask why the engagement is off,

466
00:27:24,400 --> 00:27:25,830
can I give them any reason I want?

467
00:27:26,480 --> 00:27:27,270
Sure.

468
00:27:27,960 --> 00:27:29,550
Then I'll tell them

469
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:31,030
you have bad breath, smelly feet,

470
00:27:31,400 --> 00:27:32,030
and a messy private life.

471
00:27:32,030 --> 00:27:33,000
That you like wearing T-backs,

472
00:27:33,270 --> 00:27:35,000
you're impotent, and you have an STD.

473
00:27:36,550 --> 00:27:39,590
Could you leave out the impotence and STD?

474
00:27:40,640 --> 00:27:41,310
Okay.

475
00:27:41,310 --> 00:27:43,200
Then I'll just say you have bad breath and smelly feet,

476
00:27:43,550 --> 00:27:45,480
wear T-backs, and have a messy private life.

477
00:27:45,750 --> 00:27:47,070
Fine.

478
00:27:55,070 --> 00:27:55,880
Hey.

479
00:27:58,590 --> 00:27:59,680
Be happy, okay?

480
00:28:00,400 --> 00:28:01,240
Don't worry.

481
00:28:01,240 --> 00:28:02,160
I will be.

482
00:28:19,590 --> 00:28:20,400
What's the situation?

483
00:28:20,830 --> 00:28:21,830
Is Pedro going to show?

484
00:28:22,400 --> 00:28:23,640
At noon the day after tomorrow,

485
00:28:23,750 --> 00:28:24,830
at the Eastern Hall mansion,

486
00:28:25,000 --> 00:28:26,000
Pedro will be there,

487
00:28:26,400 --> 00:28:28,590
and so will all of Eastern Hall's core members.

488
00:28:29,590 --> 00:28:31,030
We've been preparing for this moment all along.

489
00:28:31,830 --> 00:28:32,750
Stay sharp.

490
00:28:33,110 --> 00:28:34,000
Nothing can go wrong.

491
00:28:37,160 --> 00:28:38,030
Here's the recorder.

492
00:28:38,720 --> 00:28:40,440
Record every word they say.

493
00:28:41,240 --> 00:28:43,750
Every word could be crucial evidence in court.

494
00:28:51,400 --> 00:28:52,160
Okay.

495
00:28:53,240 --> 00:28:54,880
Ho Tung Fong plans to seize the printing plate

496
00:28:54,880 --> 00:28:56,440
if the talks break down.

497
00:28:56,550 --> 00:28:59,240
I'll try to keep things from escalating too quickly.

498
00:29:01,830 --> 00:29:04,270
How many officers will be outside as backup?

499
00:29:05,000 --> 00:29:08,590
The Criminal Intelligence Bureau will be monitoring the mansion from outside.

500
00:29:09,400 --> 00:29:10,590
CIB officers?

501
00:29:11,400 --> 00:29:12,590
Then who's making the arrests?

502
00:29:14,160 --> 00:29:15,030
I've discussed it with my superiors.

503
00:29:15,030 --> 00:29:16,550
We won't be making any arrests for now

504
00:29:16,640 --> 00:29:18,590
because we can't be sure the man who shows up

505
00:29:18,590 --> 00:29:20,960
is really Pedro.

506
00:29:21,160 --> 00:29:22,400
But whether he's Pedro or not,

507
00:29:22,640 --> 00:29:24,270
we're going to follow him

508
00:29:25,160 --> 00:29:27,750
and try to locate Dreamweaver's base and its members

509
00:29:27,750 --> 00:29:28,750
so we can take them all down at once.

510
00:29:30,640 --> 00:29:32,590
Then when are you planning to make the arrests?

511
00:29:34,550 --> 00:29:35,590
Don't worry.

512
00:29:35,960 --> 00:29:37,400
Once we've got Pedro under surveillance,

513
00:29:37,480 --> 00:29:38,960
I'll have other officers take over.

514
00:29:40,200 --> 00:29:42,400
Hang in there a little longer. It'll all be over soon.

515
00:29:42,830 --> 00:29:44,350
For both you and me,

516
00:29:44,960 --> 00:29:46,240
everything comes down to this operation.

517
00:29:48,400 --> 00:29:49,160
Thank you, sir.

518
00:29:54,270 --> 00:29:55,070
Looking good?

519
00:29:57,160 --> 00:29:57,960
Good luck.

520
00:30:22,000 --> 00:30:22,790
Hello?

521
00:30:23,030 --> 00:30:24,240
Hey, it's me.

522
00:30:24,590 --> 00:30:25,680
Why are you calling me?

523
00:30:27,680 --> 00:30:28,480
No reason.

524
00:30:28,960 --> 00:30:30,750
I just wanted to hear your voice.

525
00:30:31,680 --> 00:30:32,480
How bored are you?

526
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:36,160
What are you doing now?

527
00:30:36,590 --> 00:30:37,750
I just met with Officer Chan.

528
00:30:38,160 --> 00:30:40,750
I should be able to leave Eastern Hall soon.

529
00:30:41,400 --> 00:30:43,160
There's progress on the investigation?

530
00:30:43,960 --> 00:30:46,160
In a few days, I'll meet Dreamweaver's boss.

531
00:30:46,240 --> 00:30:47,480
Once we can tail him,

532
00:30:48,790 --> 00:30:51,160
this undercover operation will be over.

533
00:30:51,680 --> 00:30:52,590
What did you say?

534
00:30:53,240 --> 00:30:54,590
You're meeting Dreamweaver's boss?

535
00:30:54,880 --> 00:30:55,640
Where?

536
00:30:55,640 --> 00:30:56,480
Who else will be there?

537
00:30:56,590 --> 00:30:57,400
Is it dangerous?

538
00:30:57,790 --> 00:30:59,240
Hey, if I tell you,

539
00:30:59,240 --> 00:31:01,400
are you going to cause another mess?

540
00:31:01,880 --> 00:31:02,960
You don't need to worry.

541
00:31:02,960 --> 00:31:04,270
I can handle it myself.

542
00:31:05,160 --> 00:31:06,270
Okay.

543
00:31:07,030 --> 00:31:08,480
Whatever happens, be careful.

544
00:31:08,480 --> 00:31:09,440
Safety first.

545
00:31:09,440 --> 00:31:10,590
Don't take any risks.

546
00:31:11,240 --> 00:31:12,270
I know.

547
00:31:15,350 --> 00:31:17,590
Where will you live after you leave Eastern Hall?

548
00:31:18,790 --> 00:31:20,070
I'll go back to my old place

549
00:31:20,070 --> 00:31:21,270
or find somewhere new.

550
00:31:21,590 --> 00:31:23,070
Either way, I'm not moving in with you.

551
00:31:24,030 --> 00:31:26,000
Do you have to say no that quickly?

552
00:31:26,030 --> 00:31:27,830
Is my place that embarrassing to you now?

553
00:31:28,590 --> 00:31:31,880
Because your place is too far from my usual restaurant.

554
00:31:32,480 --> 00:31:34,240
Just because of that restaurant?

555
00:31:35,030 --> 00:31:36,350
Since you like it so much,

556
00:31:36,400 --> 00:31:37,640
when your assignment is over,

557
00:31:37,640 --> 00:31:38,880
let's go there together, okay?

558
00:31:40,440 --> 00:31:41,510
After all this hard work,

559
00:31:41,510 --> 00:31:43,200
all I get is a meal at that place?

560
00:31:44,060 --> 00:31:45,910
Well, you like it there.

561
00:31:46,750 --> 00:31:48,550
Okay, enough joking around.

562
00:31:49,240 --> 00:31:51,270
I need to go. Bye-bye.

563
00:31:52,750 --> 00:31:53,400
All right.

564
00:31:53,440 --> 00:31:54,750
I'll be waiting for good news.

565
00:33:34,480 --> 00:33:35,400
It's been a while,

566
00:33:35,550 --> 00:33:36,480
Mr. Pedro.

567
00:33:37,160 --> 00:33:37,960
Ms. Ho,

568
00:33:38,400 --> 00:33:39,270
good to see you again.

569
00:33:40,750 --> 00:33:42,750
This is my fiancé, Foon.

570
00:33:44,000 --> 00:33:44,790
Hello.

571
00:33:48,160 --> 00:33:49,030
Hello.

572
00:33:50,160 --> 00:33:51,240
Let's sit down and talk.

573
00:34:02,880 --> 00:34:04,400
Here's the printing plate you wanted.

574
00:34:16,230 --> 00:34:17,630
I can sell you the printing plate,

575
00:34:18,030 --> 00:34:21,030
but by the end of this month, Eastern Hall

576
00:34:21,030 --> 00:34:23,190
must deliver 500 million USD worth of goods to me.

577
00:34:24,030 --> 00:34:27,590
Starting next month, you'll deliver twice that amount.

578
00:34:28,960 --> 00:34:31,760
Of course, you'll be paid in full.

579
00:34:34,550 --> 00:34:35,400
Well?

580
00:34:36,070 --> 00:34:37,030
Any objections?

581
00:34:37,590 --> 00:34:39,030
I have a proposal

582
00:34:39,480 --> 00:34:40,630
for our future cooperation.

583
00:34:41,670 --> 00:34:44,590
I want you to sell Eastern Hall two printing plates outright

584
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:46,800
so that the counterfeit money business in Hong Kong, China

585
00:34:46,800 --> 00:34:48,360
will be entirely ours to handle from now on.

586
00:34:49,400 --> 00:34:52,230
What's in it for me?

587
00:34:52,550 --> 00:34:54,440
We'll give Dreamweaver a cut.

588
00:34:54,590 --> 00:34:56,150
You won't have to do anything

589
00:34:56,440 --> 00:34:57,590
except collect the money.

590
00:34:57,800 --> 00:34:59,280
How is that any different from now?

591
00:35:00,030 --> 00:35:01,280
We know this business inside out now.

592
00:35:01,880 --> 00:35:03,000
Leave it to us,

593
00:35:03,400 --> 00:35:04,800
and the operation will only keep growing.

594
00:35:07,000 --> 00:35:08,880
Do you really think I don't know

595
00:35:09,000 --> 00:35:10,840
there was a problem with your last shipment?

596
00:35:11,760 --> 00:35:13,400
You couldn't even handle something that simple,

597
00:35:14,630 --> 00:35:16,960
and you think you can expand the operation?

598
00:35:17,280 --> 00:35:19,400
I hope you'll seriously consider it.

599
00:35:20,630 --> 00:35:23,800
I believe this is the best decision for all of us.

600
00:35:24,360 --> 00:35:25,550
I'm not interested.

601
00:35:25,710 --> 00:35:27,360
Anyone who works with me

602
00:35:28,070 --> 00:35:29,760
plays by my rules.

603
00:35:38,440 --> 00:35:40,630
So you asked me here for a face-to-face handover

604
00:35:42,440 --> 00:35:43,590
because you wanted to force my hand.

605
00:35:45,190 --> 00:35:46,700
If you want this to end peacefully,

606
00:35:47,360 --> 00:35:48,360
leave the printing plate.

607
00:35:53,000 --> 00:35:56,270
I put a lot of effort into helping you become the leader.

608
00:35:57,590 --> 00:35:59,550
I thought we could work together for a long time.

609
00:35:59,800 --> 00:36:01,070
Make your choice.

610
00:36:01,800 --> 00:36:02,800
Save the talk.

611
00:36:03,070 --> 00:36:04,000
If you want to work with me,

612
00:36:05,000 --> 00:36:07,000
you have to keep your promises.

613
00:36:08,030 --> 00:36:09,840
I'm sure you've heard

614
00:36:09,840 --> 00:36:12,800
what happens to people who fail to meet my demands.

615
00:36:33,400 --> 00:36:34,190
Ms. Ho,

616
00:36:35,360 --> 00:36:36,880
it's been a pleasure knowing you.

617
00:36:37,360 --> 00:36:38,150
Shawn.

618
00:36:41,000 --> 00:36:42,590
Eastern Hall has considerable influence.

619
00:36:42,760 --> 00:36:45,000
I'm sure there are still ways we can help Dreamweaver.

620
00:36:49,000 --> 00:36:50,840
Spare Ms. Ho,

621
00:36:51,000 --> 00:36:54,000
and we'll help Dreamweaver grow even bigger.

622
00:36:59,610 --> 00:37:01,170
You make a good point, Foon Gor.

623
00:37:02,670 --> 00:37:04,280
I can spare your lives,

624
00:37:04,400 --> 00:37:05,670
but I have one condition.

625
00:37:06,800 --> 00:37:07,800
You

626
00:37:08,400 --> 00:37:09,630
have to come with me.

627
00:37:16,840 --> 00:37:17,630
Okay.

628
00:37:18,150 --> 00:37:19,030
No problem.

629
00:37:24,480 --> 00:37:25,280
It's okay.

630
00:37:38,150 --> 00:37:38,960
Foon Gor,

631
00:37:40,030 --> 00:37:41,440
bear with this for a bit.

632
00:38:05,330 --> 00:38:06,130
Boss.

633
00:38:10,150 --> 00:38:11,000
This morning,

634
00:38:11,000 --> 00:38:13,480
a fatal shooting occurred at a detached house in the New Territories.

635
00:38:13,840 --> 00:38:16,150
Regional Crime Unit officers rushed to the scene.

636
00:38:16,150 --> 00:38:16,960
So far,

637
00:38:17,000 --> 00:38:18,360
five people have been confirmed dead

638
00:38:18,360 --> 00:38:19,190
and several others injured.

639
00:38:19,320 --> 00:38:21,230
All the injured have been taken to hospital for emergency treatment.

640
00:38:21,230 --> 00:38:22,030
Sources say

641
00:38:22,030 --> 00:38:23,960
all the injured are members of Eastern Hall.

642
00:38:24,230 --> 00:38:26,070
Police have not ruled out

643
00:38:26,070 --> 00:38:27,800
a dispute between gangs as the cause.

644
00:38:27,840 --> 00:38:30,070
We'll continue to bring you updates as the investigation develops.

645
00:38:32,000 --> 00:38:34,270
In a few days, I'll meet Dreamweaver's boss.

646
00:38:34,280 --> 00:38:35,790
Once we can tail him,

647
00:38:36,840 --> 00:38:39,190
this undercover operation will be over.

648
00:38:45,190 --> 00:38:47,840
Hi, I can't take your call right now.

649
00:38:48,030 --> 00:38:50,510
Leave me a message after the beep.

650
00:39:06,760 --> 00:39:07,550
Welcome.

651
00:39:08,150 --> 00:39:08,960
Sorry.

652
00:39:09,110 --> 00:39:10,360
I put you through a lot.

653
00:39:13,110 --> 00:39:14,190
Where am I?

654
00:39:14,440 --> 00:39:15,400
My place.

655
00:39:16,190 --> 00:39:17,000
Foon Gor,

656
00:39:17,630 --> 00:39:19,400
now you can finally stay by my side.

657
00:39:20,480 --> 00:39:22,000
Stay by your side?

658
00:39:27,640 --> 00:39:32,850
[Episode 7]

659
00:39:32,940 --> 00:39:48,670
[This story is fictional. Any resemblance is entirely coincidental.]
